<title>UK: EIB prices $1.0 billion 10-year bond, +17 bp.</title>
<headline>EIB prices $1.0 billion 10-year bond, +17 bp.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Investment Bank's</p>
<p>$1.0 billion 10-year global bond has been priced, joint lead</p>
<p>managers CS First Boston and Lehman Brothers said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The deal was launched on Tuesday.</p>
<p>+ + +</p>
<p> AMT	  $1.0 BLN  COUPON     7.125     MATURITY    18.SEP.06</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.979    PAY DATE    18.SEP.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.325     REOFFER    99.979    SPREAD	+17 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 1	   SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  SUPRA     TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.125     SELL CONC  20	  PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 7.00 PCT U.S. TREASURY NOTE DUE 15.JUL.06 -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
